WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.660
During the DC FanDome digital event in late
August 2020, Warner Bros. released the first

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:10.640
trailer for The Batman, the upcoming 2021
feature that stars Robert Pattinson as a younger,

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.200
even broodier Dark Knight.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.960
While the trailer doesn't give away much,
seeing how only 25 percent of the film was

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:20.289
shot before the pandemic halted production,
it's peppered with numerous clues and at least

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:24.080
one big, secret tease that possibly hints
toward a grander conspiracy.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.820
The Batman writer-director Matt Reeves hinted
at such when he spoke at DC FanDome, teasing

00:00:28.829 --> 00:00:32.500
that the film will peel back the layers of
Batman's origins and take a closer look at

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.880
Bruce Wayne's family, particularly what role
they played in Gotham City declining into

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:37.500
corruption.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:43.000
"You start to see as it starts to describe
this epic history of corruption in Gotham,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.900
that you start to understand, 'Well, where
did my family sit in that?'"

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:51.260
Reeves' statement, revealing that the movie
will touch on Bruce Wayne's origins and question

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:54.630
what involvement his family might have had
in corrupting Gotham in the first place, has

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.200
set the internet ablaze with a mind-blowing
theory.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.520
While there's almost certainly some degree
of misdirection going on, if you take The

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:04.140
Batman trailer at face value there are several
big takeaways presented.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.040
One, the Riddler is the central antagonist,
and he seems to be taking things a little

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.540
bit more seriously this time.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.600
"Does anybody else feel like a fried egg?!"

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:17.240
Two, this is a younger, angrier Bruce Wayne,
still learning the ropes of this whole "being

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.340
a vigilante" thing.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.500
And three, the Riddler, for whatever reason,
is not only leaving clues for the Batman,

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.050
but also creepy personal messages, foreshadowing
a personal vendetta that seems to be a mystery

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.100
for even Bruce Wayne.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.500
"You're a part of this, too."

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.060
"How am I a part of it?"

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.520
"You'll see."

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:41.900
From here, many fans have theorized that a
deeper conspiracy is afoot, one that revolves

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:45.700
around the Riddler potentially knowing far
more about the Batman than he lets on.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.960
There's some basis for this in the comics:
The Riddler is often presented as a brilliant

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:54.270
but socially awkward manipulator who plays
people like chess pieces, albeit in weird

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:54.900
ways.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.260
In the storyline "Hush," he deduces Batman's
secret identity.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.760
So, what if he's done the same thing in The
Batman?

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:05.200
What if the Riddler knows Bruce Wayne is Batman,
using that information as a motivator in his

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.340
twisted games?

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:10.400
Well, if this ends up being true in The Batman,
the classic narrative of the Riddler leaving

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.720
clues out of an abstract, intellectual desire
to match wits with an equal might be completely

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.480
upended.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:19.140
Furthermore, if this theory is correct, then
the Riddler isn't just leaving riddles to

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.500
tease Bruce about knowing his weird little
nighttime habit, he has bigger ambitions.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.000
What ambitions, though?

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.900
As a number of eagle-eyed fans have noted,
the trailer for The Batman depicts the Riddler

00:02:28.911 --> 00:02:33.130
leaving Batman a card with an owl on the front,
and that points them to another area of the

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.140
Waynes' lives that the Riddler might know
about.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.920
"How did you figure this out?"

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:42.360
The Batman has consistently been described
as more of a noir-inspired mystery film than

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:43.840
the character's previous movies.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.700
With that framework in mind, every clue matters.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.020
The choice to use owl imagery is probably
not an Easter egg, but rather, a clue toward

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:56.030
the involvement of the Court of Owls, a secret
society comprised of Gotham's wealthiest leaders,

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.540
businessmen, and politicians.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:01.700
In the comics, the Court of Owls have spent
centuries controlling Gotham's underbelly,

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:05.810
enforcing the wealth inequality, crime, and
corruption that make the city so infamous.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:10.239
Now, remember what Reeves said before regarding
Batman being forced to question where his

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:14.440
family sat in Gotham's history of corruption:
The odds are, given all this, that the Waynes

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:17.540
have a bloodier history than Bruce's parents
might've ever told him.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:21.470
And while the comics have generally depicted
Thomas and Martha Wayne as being charitable

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.750
and decent figures, whom the Court of Owls
directly opposed, the same might not be true

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:26.440
in this film.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:30.200
It's entirely possible that they may have
even been members of the Court of Owls, or

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.580
perhaps supported the organization's goals,
knowingly or unknowingly.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:37.900
Alternatively, their opposition to the Court's
corruption might have, in this movie at least,

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.340
directly led to their deaths.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.600
"It's got of course action, and, you know,
all that kind of stuff, but at the end of

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.521
it, it also is incredibly personal for him,
even though it is this story in which he is

00:03:46.521 --> 00:03:48.700
trying to understand and unravel this mystery."

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:52.900
Either way, the Riddler's statement that "You're
a part of this, too," implies that the entire

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:57.320
goal of his puzzles might be to force Bruce
Wayne to confront his family's dark past.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:01.631
And if this hypothesis actually proves accurate,
it still remains to be seen where the Riddler

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.060
stands on all of this.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:06.560
Is he serving the Court of Owls, for instance,
or trying to take them down?

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.460
Who knows?

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:09.320
All of this might be wrong, anyway.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:11.020
In the meantime, it's fun to speculate.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:12.400
"What does it mean?"

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.020
"It's a riddle."

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:18.140
The Batman hits theaters on October 1, 2021.

